WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.094
For the next week, Ben went to rehearsal every day after school.

2
00:00:10.095 --> 00:00:15.399
Luckily, there were no new disasters.

3
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.472
But on the following Monday, after Ben had finished his scenes, Victoria frowned at him.

4
00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:27.398
"You're doing well, Ben. But I want you off book by our next rehearsal."

5
00:00:27.399 --> 00:00:31.588
Ben looked at her, confused.

6
00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:35.886
"I'm not on a book, Ms. Lafang."

7
00:00:35.887 --> 00:00:38.478
She laughed loudly.

8
00:00:38.479 --> 00:00:43.900
"Silly ghost! 'Off book' means your lines are memorized.

9
00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:48.237
Once you've got them memorized, we can start focusing on acting technique."

10
00:00:48.238 --> 00:00:53.100
She waved Waldo over.

11
00:00:53.101 --> 00:00:56.634
"Waldo, can you please help Ben learn his lines?"

12
00:00:56.635 --> 00:00:59.553
"Sure thing," Waldo said. "Let's

13
00:00:59.554 --> 00:01:04.247
go to the science lab, Ben. It'll be quieter there." ***

14
00:01:04.248 --> 00:01:08.378
Ben and Waldo worked on Ben's lines for the rest of the afternoon.

15
00:01:08.379 --> 00:01:13.126
Ben was trying hard, but before long, he felt exasperated.

16
00:01:13.127 --> 00:01:17.071
"I can't remember my lines, Waldo." Ben shook his head.

17
00:01:17.072 --> 00:01:19.056
"What's wrong with me?"

18
00:01:19.057 --> 00:01:21.861
"Try again," Waldo said.

19
00:01:21.862 --> 00:01:26.004
"'So foul and far a day—'"

20
00:01:26.005 --> 00:01:32.515
Waldo stopped him. "It's 'So foul and fair a day.'"

21
00:01:32.516 --> 00:01:35.492
"This is hopeless!" Ben cried.

22
00:01:35.493 --> 00:01:36.982
"You were right about me.

23
00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:43.237
I'm not good at memorizing stuff, and I never should have auditioned for the play!"

24
00:01:43.238 --> 00:01:50.112
"Actually . . ." Waldo looked around the lab. "I think I can help."

25
00:01:50.113 --> 00:01:52.177
"Huh?"

26
00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.797
"I'll make a memory potion."

27
00:01:55.798 --> 00:02:01.901
"No way!" Ben thought, looking down to hide his expression.

28
00:02:01.902 --> 00:02:07.231
Waldo's spells were nearly always a disaster.

29
00:02:07.232 --> 00:02:10.698
"Thanks, but I'll just keep working on my lines."

30
00:02:10.699 --> 00:02:19.277
Waldo nodded. "Okay, but if you change your mind, let me know."

31
00:02:19.278 --> 00:02:22.107
*** "I'm home, Uncle Bert," Ben

32
00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:27.416
called. "I'll be in my room, working on my lines." But Uncle Bert didn't

33
00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:29.983
respond. "Where are you?" Ben

34
00:02:29.984 --> 00:02:31.641
called. He checked the

35
00:02:31.642 --> 00:02:34.534
kitchen. No one was

36
00:02:34.535 --> 00:02:38.104
there. The living room was empty, and so was the family room.

37
00:02:38.105 --> 00:02:41.429
Even Sid wasn't there.

38
00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:51.111
"This is weird," Ben said, and then he smelled it—a stink coming in through the screen door.

39
00:02:51.112 --> 00:02:53.691
"Eww, what is that?"

40
00:02:53.692 --> 00:03:00.585
He floated into the backyard, trying to follow the scent, when Bones came bounding up.

41
00:03:00.586 --> 00:03:07.576
"Hi, boy!" As Ben reached down to pet his dog, he got a face full of a foul odor.

42
00:03:07.577 --> 00:03:13.914
"Whoa, Bones! Did you get sprayed by a skunk monster again?"

43
00:03:13.915 --> 00:03:17.977
Bones yipped happily and tried to rub up against Ben's leg.

44
00:03:17.978 --> 00:03:22.479
"Oh no, you don't," Ben said. "It's bath time for you."

45
00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.477
Bones lay down at Ben's feet and covered his eyes with his paws.

46
00:03:27.478 --> 00:03:29.576
"I know," Ben said.

47
00:03:29.577 --> 00:03:34.656
"I hate dog baths too. Let's get it over with."

48
00:03:34.657 --> 00:03:38.109
*** Bathing Bones took longer than Ben thought it

49
00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:43.854
would. By the time he'd washed skunk spray off Bones, it was almost

50
00:03:43.855 --> 00:03:48.446
dinnertime. Ben poured himself a glass of sludge and sat down to study his

51
00:03:48.447 --> 00:03:54.333
script. Then Uncle Bert and Sid floated in with bags of

52
00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:57.984
groceries. "I'm glad you're home, Ben," Uncle Bert

53
00:03:57.985 --> 00:04:00.735
said. "Sid has a school project to

54
00:04:00.736 --> 00:04:03.607
complete. Please help him while I make

55
00:04:03.608 --> 00:04:08.633
dinner." "Can't you do it yourself, Sid?" Ben asked. "I have to learn my lines."

56
00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:10.826
"Nope." Sid shook his head.

57
00:04:10.827 --> 00:04:16.315
"I need help—and Mom told Uncle Bert that you have to help me."

58
00:04:16.316 --> 00:04:25.280
Sid yanked on Ben's arm. "Let's go."

59
00:04:25.281 --> 00:04:28.955
*** After dinner Ben pulled out the script

60
00:04:28.956 --> 00:04:32.124
again. Then he got a text from his mom: "Don't

61
00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:37.119
forget. You promised to feed the neighbors' bat and clean their tarantula's

62
00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.056
cage." "Oh no!" Ben

63
00:04:42.057 --> 00:04:47.345
groaned. The chore was another thing he hadn't

64
00:04:47.346 --> 00:04:52.833
remembered! Another hour passed before Ben finally collapsed on his bed, script in

65
00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:56.789
hand. Uncle Bert knocked on the door and poked his head

66
00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:01.166
inside. "Everything okay, Ben? You looked a little pale at

67
00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:04.637
dinner. Didn't you like my spiderweb

68
00:05:04.638 --> 00:05:09.288
soufflé?" Ben sighed. "It was

69
00:05:09.289 --> 00:05:12.795
great. But I have to memorize my lines, and I'm having a hard

70
00:05:12.796 --> 00:05:16.169
time." "You sound just like me," Uncle Bert

71
00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:21.082
said. "Did I ever tell you that I was once cast in the lead part in a school

72
00:05:21.083 --> 00:05:24.053
play?" Ben shook his

73
00:05:24.054 --> 00:05:31.829
head. "Yep, and it was opposite the most beautiful monster in school." Uncle Bert

74
00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:39.654
grinned. "I had the biggest crush on her, but I couldn't talk to her without stuttering and acting like a fool.

75
00:05:39.655 --> 00:05:46.474
And then being in the play with her made me so nervous, I couldn't remember a single line!"

76
00:05:46.475 --> 00:05:51.113
"So what happened?" Ben asked. "How'd you finally memorize your lines?"

77
00:05:51.114 --> 00:05:52.828
Uncle Bert shrugged.

78
00:05:52.829 --> 00:05:58.493
"Actually, I never did memorize them—the director replaced me with another actor.

79
00:05:58.494 --> 00:06:01.607
But that won't happen to you. Now sleep well."

80
00:06:01.608 --> 00:06:05.615
And with that, Uncle Bert floated out of Ben's room.

81
00:06:05.616 --> 00:06:12.987
Ben groaned. "That was the least inspiring story I've ever heard," he thought.

82
00:06:12.988 --> 00:06:17.662
He reached for his phone.

83
00:06:17.663 --> 00:06:23.148
Hey, Waldo. Looks like I'm going to need a potion after all.

